From 6e98c69a2f1fedca22f5c11b608e16e5185f22c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): hold a merged Gateway delivery in one stable
 release-deferred state while the release path is disabled (JAM B12)

A merged ai.ubq.fi delivery whose source issue closed through its closing
keyword waits at `delivery` beside its open production release request.
The release path is disabled (the VPS release contract is an open owner
decision, #10, #13, #152), so the release ref holds no VPS release record
and `observeGatewayVpsDelivery` can only answer `wait`. R80's
`waitRelease` re-armed a five-minute `unavailable` wait for each such
record on every runtime cycle: live 670 rewrote it 138 times, and 348 of
632 repair-state commits between 2026-10-17T16:34Z and 20:36Z were these
re-arms of 25 records, each spending a delivery-bucket step. The launcher's
closure-delivery pass also ran the full closure gate (task, opt-out, pull
and two release reads) for each record and printed one
`delivery:<id>:release_unavailable` line per record per pass.

Runtime (src/): when the open request has no VPS release record on a
release ref that reads back cleanly (`gatewayReleaseDeferred`), the
delivery step writes one open-ended `unavailable` wait at `delivery`
(`deferRelease`). Selection skips it, so after that one write the record
takes no step and no write. Once per run, and only when such a record
exists, `resumeDeferredRelease` reads the release ref once. It releases
the wait of a record whose request the release ref now records, whose
request is no longer open, or that holds an intent. The ordinary step then
observes the outcome on the same run. Each record is looked at once per
run. A cancelled or failed request is never deferred.

The record is not marked done. The VPS controller begins open requests
without reading the work record, but only the record consumes the outcome:
acceptance reconciles the closure, and a failed or rolled-back release
blocks it. Both the runtime's `observeReleaseAcceptance` and the
launcher's `gatewayClosureGate` bind only a record at `delivery`, and a
done record never moves again.

Launcher (ops/): such a delivery is counted in one line per pass,
`release-deferred:count=<n>:release_path=disabled` (`queued` once VPS
release records exist but none for these requests). Nothing is read for it
in the closure-delivery, retirement or foreign-closure loops; its request
was recorded only after the merge, so it is never closed unmerged. The
check reads the snapshots and never the wait, so it applies to R80's waits
as well as the new shape. The full gate runs again once the release ref
records the request.

R80 compatibility: no generation-80 path writes an open-ended
`unavailable` wait. R80 parses the new shape, its selection skips it, and
its cycles write nothing over it. The live launcher 3f041b46d never reads
the wait: it reports `release_unavailable` over the new shape and writes
nothing. An accepted release still closes the deferred record out to
`done` through any launcher's closure gate. No state field, blocker or
runtime stdout line is added.

